<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>Compress Images: third-party licenses</title>
    <style>
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
            body {
                background: #333;
                color: white;
            }
            a {
                color: skyblue;
            }
        }
        .container {
            font-family: sans-serif;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }
        .intro {
            text-align: center;
        }
        .licenses-list {
            list-style-type: none;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }
        .license-used-by {
            margin-top: -10px;
        }
        .license-text {
            max-height: 200px;
            overflow-y: scroll;
            white-space: pre-wrap;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <main class="container">
        <div class="intro">
            <h1>Third-Party Licenses</h1>
            <p>Compress Images is licensed under GPL-3.0-only. It includes the projects below.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>Native libraries</h2>
        <p>C libraries compiled into, or shipped with, the release builds (in addition to the
        Rust crates listed further down, some of which bundle C code of their own):</p>
        <ul>
            <li><b>libimagequant</b> (lossy PNG): GPL-3.0-or-later. <a href="https://pngquant.org/lib/">pngquant.org/lib</a></li>
            <li><b>mozjpeg</b> (JPEG encoder): IJG, BSD-3-Clause and Zlib. <a href="https://github.com/mozilla/mozjpeg">github.com/mozilla/mozjpeg</a></li>
            <li><b>libwebp</b> (WebP): BSD-3-Clause. <a href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/webm/libwebp">chromium.googlesource.com/webm/libwebp</a></li>
            <li><b>libheif</b> (HEIC input; Windows and Linux builds): LGPL-3.0-or-later. <a href="https://github.com/strukturag/libheif">github.com/strukturag/libheif</a></li>
            <li><b>libde265</b> (HEVC decoder for HEIC; Windows and Linux builds): LGPL-3.0-or-later. <a href="https://github.com/strukturag/libde265">github.com/strukturag/libde265</a></li>
            <li><b>x265</b> (linked into libheif on Windows, not used for decoding): GPL-2.0-or-later. <a href="https://bitbucket.org/multicoreware/x265_git">bitbucket.org/multicoreware/x265_git</a></li>
            <li><b>dav1d</b> (AV1 decoder for AVIF input; Windows and Linux builds): BSD-2-Clause. <a href="https://code.videolan.org/videolan/dav1d">code.videolan.org/videolan/dav1d</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p>On macOS, HEIC and AVIF are decoded by the operating system. The desktop app's
        interface is built with Svelte (MIT) and the Tauri JavaScript API (Apache-2.0 / MIT).
        Complete license texts for all of the above are in their source repositories.</p>
    
        <h2>Overview of licenses:</h2>
        <ul class="licenses-overview">
            {{#each overview}}
            <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
            {{/each}}
        </ul>

        <h2>All license text:</h2>
        <ul class="licenses-list">
            {{#each licenses}}
            <li class="license">
                <h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
                <h4>Used by:</h4>
                <ul class="license-used-by">
                    {{#each used_by}}
                    <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}} {{crate.repository}} {{else}} https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}} {{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
                    {{/each}}
                </ul>
                <pre class="license-text">{{text}}</pre>
            </li>
            {{/each}}
        </ul>
    </main>
</body>

</html>
